; `uint .size (l..h)` with a NONZERO lower size. RFC 8610 §3.8.1 defines `.size` on `uint` only as
; a maximum byte count, so the lower bound has two readings (0, or 256**(l-1)) and neither oracle
; implements the ranged form; refused gracefully. It once generated `256..65535` (a `2**(8*l)`
; lower bound matching neither reading). The zero-lower-size form maps onto the plain window and
; is pinned by `robustness_tests::uint_size_range_lower_bound`.
x = uint .size (1..2)
